      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really interesting distinction. so if it's less about corporate contracts and more about \"blood and honor,\" how does that affect the profile of the people he recruits? i'm trying to see if there's a specific \"archetype\" for his subordinates based on those cultural pressures. for example, would his crew naturally be composed of certain types of people from his community because of those shared cultural values or shared struggle? i want to avoid making him just a lone wolf—i need to understand if his organization reflects a specific cultural way of operating that sets them apart from other types of organized crime.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
